  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the set $X={2,4,6,8,10,12,14}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n{{2,4,8},{6,12},\\,{10},\\,____\\,}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $2\\in {2,4,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $4\\in {2,4,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $6\\in {6,12}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $8\\in {2,4,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $10\\in {10}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $12\\in {6,12}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $14$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe element $14$ is not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${14}.$",
